<% content_for :title, "Demo 2: Using Swagger Files" %>

<div class="container py-5">

  <%# Back to Home %>
  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col">
      <%= link_to root_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" do %>
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i> Back to Demo Selection
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Hero Section %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-8 mx-auto text-center">
      <span class="badge bg-primary mb-3">Demo 2</span>
      <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">
        <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-code text-primary me-2"></i>
        Using Swagger Files
      </h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted">
        Learn how to convert OpenAPI/Swagger specifications into advanced functions automatically.
        This approach saves time when integrating APIs with existing documentation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Why Use Swagger Files Card %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-primary">
        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-question-circle me-2"></i>
            Why Use Swagger Files?
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="mb-3">
            Swagger (OpenAPI) files are standardized specifications that describe REST APIs. Using them with AIsuru offers several advantages:
          </p>
          <ul class="mb-0">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Automatic generation:</strong> Create multiple advanced functions at once instead of configuring them manually one by one
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Consistency:</strong> All endpoints, parameters, and response formats are already documented and standardized
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Time-saving:</strong> Perfect for integrating complex APIs with many endpoints
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Accuracy:</strong> Reduces errors by using the official API specification directly
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Instructions Card %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-info">
        <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2"></i>
            Step-by-Step Guide
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3">Part 1: Download the Swagger File</h6>
          <ol class="mb-4">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Download the <code>swaggerfile_aisuru.json</code></strong> file from the course materials:
              <div class="mt-2">
                <%= link_to download_swagger_demo2_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary" do %>
                  <i class="bi bi-download me-1"></i>
                  Download swaggerfile_aisuru.json
                <% end %>
              </div>
              <small class="text-muted d-block mt-2">
                <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
                This file contains the OpenAPI specification for the AIsuru engine API
              </small>
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Save the file</strong> to your computer in an easily accessible location
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3 mt-4">Part 2: Create the Agent</h6>
          <ol start="3" class="mb-4">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Create a new Agent</strong> on the AIsuru Platform (or use an existing one)
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3 mt-4">Part 3: Import the Swagger File</h6>
          <ol start="4" class="mb-4">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Navigate to Advanced Functions</strong> in the left sidebar
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Click on "Converti OpenAPI in funzioni"</strong> (Convert OpenAPI to functions)
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Configure the import:</strong>
              <ul class="mt-2">
                <li><strong>URL base del webhook:</strong> <code>https://engine.memori.ai</code></li>
                <li><strong>Upload file:</strong> Select the <code>swaggerfile_aisuru.json</code> file you downloaded</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Click "Import"</strong> to generate the functions automatically
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Review the generated functions:</strong> AIsuru will create multiple advanced functions based on the API endpoints defined in the Swagger file
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3 mt-4">Part 4: Get Your Agent IDs</h6>
          <ol start="9" class="mb-0">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Open your Agent</strong> and click on <strong>"Dev docs"</strong> in the left sidebar
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              Expand the <strong>"▼ Other references"</strong> section
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              Copy the following values:
              <ul class="mt-2">
                <li><strong>Secondary Memori (Agent) ID</strong> → This is your <code>memoriID</code></li>
                <li><strong>Owner user ID</strong> → This is your <code>ownerUserID</code></li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Paste them in the form below</strong> to test your agent
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Configuration Form %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card shadow">
        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-gear me-2"></i>
            Configure Your Agent
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <%= form_with url: demo2_configure_path, method: :post, local: true do |f| %>
            <div class="mb-4">
              <label for="memori_id" class="form-label fw-bold">
                <i class="bi bi-fingerprint me-1"></i>
                Memori ID (Secondary Agent ID)
              </label>
              <%= f.text_field :memori_id,
                  class: "form-control form-control-lg",
                  placeholder: "e.g., a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
                  required: true,
                  pattern: "[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}" %>
              <div class="form-text">
                Found in Dev docs → Other references → "Secondary Memori (Agent) ID"
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-4">
              <label for="owner_user_id" class="form-label fw-bold">
                <i class="bi bi-person-badge me-1"></i>
                Owner User ID
              </label>
              <%= f.text_field :owner_user_id,
                  class: "form-control form-control-lg",
                  placeholder: "e.g., b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
                  required: true,
                  pattern: "[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}" %>
              <div class="form-text">
                Found in Dev docs → Other references → "Owner user ID"
              </div>
            </div>

            <hr class="my-4">
            <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">
              <i class="bi bi-sliders me-1"></i>
              Advanced Configuration (pre-filled with defaults)
            </h6>

            <div class="row">
              <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                <label for="tenant_id" class="form-label">
                  <i class="bi bi-building me-1"></i>
                  Tenant ID
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :tenant_id,
                    class: "form-control",
                    value: @tenant_id || "www.aisuru.com",
                    required: true %>
              </div>

              <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                <label for="base_url" class="form-label">
                  <i class="bi bi-link-45deg me-1"></i>
                  Base URL
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :base_url,
                    class: "form-control",
                    value: @base_url || "https://www.aisuru.com",
                    required: true %>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-3">
              <label for="engine_url" class="form-label">
                <i class="bi bi-cpu me-1"></i>
                Engine URL
              </label>
              <%= f.text_field :engine_url,
                  class: "form-control",
                  value: @engine_url || "https://engine.memori.ai/memori/v2",
                  required: true %>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-4">
              <label for="api_url" class="form-label">
                <i class="bi bi-server me-1"></i>
                API URL
              </label>
              <%= f.text_field :api_url,
                  class: "form-control",
                  value: @api_url || "https://backend.memori.ai/api/v2",
                  required: true %>
            </div>

            <div class="d-grid">
              <%= f.submit "Load Agent", class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if @show_agent %>
    <%# Agent Success Alert %>
    <div class="row mb-4">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="alert alert-success d-flex align-items-center">
          <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2 fs-4"></i>
          <div>
            <strong>Agent Loaded!</strong>
            Test your agent with the functions imported from the Swagger file.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Web Component %>
    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card shadow">
          <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
            <h5 class="mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-robot me-2"></i>
              Your AIsuru Agent
            </h5>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body p-0">
            <div class="memori-container">
              <memori-client
                memoriName="SwaggerAgent"
                ownerUserName="owner"
                memoriID="<%= @memori_id %>"
                ownerUserID="<%= @owner_user_id %>"
                tenantID="<%= @tenant_id %>"
                engineURL="<%= @engine_url %>"
                apiURL="<%= @api_url %>"
                baseURL="<%= @base_url %>"
                layout="CHAT"
                uiLang="EN"
                spokenLang="EN"
                showLogin="true"
              ></memori-client>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Code Example %>
    <div class="row mb-4">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card border-dark">
          <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">
            <h6 class="mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-file-code me-2"></i>
              HTML Code Example
            </h6>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body bg-light">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>&lt;!-- Include AIsuru Web Component --&gt;
&lt;script type="module" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@memori.ai/memori-webcomponent/dist/memori-webcomponent.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@memori.ai/memori-react/dist/styles.min.css" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Configure your agent --&gt;
&lt;memori-client
  memoriName="SwaggerAgent"
  ownerUserName="owner"
  memoriID="<%= @memori_id %>"
  ownerUserID="<%= @owner_user_id %>"
  tenantID="<%= @tenant_id %>"
  engineURL="<%= @engine_url %>"
  apiURL="<%= @api_url %>"
  baseURL="<%= @base_url %>"
  layout="CHAT"
  uiLang="EN"
  spokenLang="EN"
  showLogin="true"
&gt;&lt;/memori-client&gt;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# Info Cards %>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
      <div class="card h-100 card-hover border-0 shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-body text-center p-4">
          <i class="bi bi-lightning-charge display-4 text-primary mb-3"></i>
          <h5 class="card-title">Rapid Development</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Import dozens of functions in seconds instead of creating them manually one by one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
      <div class="card h-100 card-hover border-0 shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-body text-center p-4">
          <i class="bi bi-shield-check display-4 text-success mb-3"></i>
          <h5 class="card-title">Standardized</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            OpenAPI is an industry standard, ensuring compatibility and accurate API definitions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
      <div class="card h-100 card-hover border-0 shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-body text-center p-4">
          <i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat display-4 text-info mb-3"></i>
          <h5 class="card-title">Easy Updates</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            When the API changes, simply re-import the updated Swagger file to sync your functions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Additional Tips %>
  <div class="row mt-4">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-warning">
        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
          <h6 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-2"></i>
            Tips & Best Practices
          </h6>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <ul class="mb-0">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Review imported functions:</strong> After importing, review the generated functions to understand what endpoints are available.
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Select only what you need:</strong> You don't have to enable all imported functions - choose only those relevant to your agent's purpose.
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Check the base URL:</strong> Make sure the webhook base URL matches the actual API endpoint (in this case, <code>https://engine.memori.ai</code>).
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Update your prompt:</strong> After importing functions, update your agent's prompt to explain when and how to use each function.
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <strong>Version control:</strong> Keep track of which Swagger file version you imported, especially if the API evolves over time.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
